/target
.metrics
*.tar.gz
!Cargo.lock
# release binary copied out of the build container for live checks. Named after the package, so a
# rename of the directory had to be repeated here: a stale entry ignores a file that no longer
# exists and lets the real binary be committed.
/rrl-directory
# redb files seeded for live checks
/build
.#*
ldapsearch
ldapmodify
ldapadd
ldaputil
ldapdelete
ldapmodrdn
ldapcompare
ldapwhoami
ldappasswd
# Fuzzing: the corpus is generated (tens of megabytes in minutes) and the artifacts are crash
# inputs, kept only while one is being investigated. What is committed is fuzz/seeds.
/fuzz/corpus
/fuzz/artifacts
/fuzz/target
# cargo-mutants writes its report here; the next run rotates the previous to `mutants.out.old`
# instead of deleting it, so the pattern covers both.
/mutants.out*

# A developer's own arrangement for building against locally checked-out siblings — the `[patch]`
# blocks that used to sit in Cargo.toml and broke every clean checkout. Ignored, not committed: the
# manifest has to describe a build that works from a bare clone.
/.cargo/config.toml

# Python bytecode from the acceptance script
__pycache__/
*.pyc
